# A source control presents one buffer at a time. Its project always owns the
# main document, so opening a definition never changes Run, Save or Share.
import source_workspace.dl
import text.dl
import focus.dl

to get [the UI source buffer for] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor}:
    require condition (document's project = editor's document's project) reporting "A source view cannot display another editor's project"
    set buffer to editor's buffers
    loop while buffer != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source buffer):
        if buffer's document = document:
            return buffer
        set buffer to buffer's next
    set buffer to storage for one slot initialized with (a new UI source buffer)
    set buffer's document to document
    set buffer's state's text to document's source
    set buffer's next to editor's buffers
    set editor's buffers to buffer
    return buffer

to [remember the UI source location of] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set buffer to editor's current
    set layout to the UI layout for element (editor's node) in (view's layout)
    require condition (layout != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "A source view is missing its layout"
    if view's selection's caret source = (the address of (layout's text source)):
        set buffer's caret to view's selection's caret
        if view's selection's anchor source = view's selection's caret source:
            set buffer's anchor to view's selection's anchor
        else:
            set buffer's anchor to buffer's caret
    set buffer's horizontal to layout's text scroll
    set buffer's vertical to layout's scroll position

to [restore UI source location] {a pointer to UI source buffer:buffer} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    require condition (editor's current = buffer) reporting "Only the visible source buffer can receive focus"
    set layout to the UI layout for element (editor's node) in (view's layout)
    require condition (layout != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "A source view is missing its layout"
    set text to (the UI value for (editor's node) in (view's instance))'s text
    set source to the address of (layout's text source)
    if source's text != text:
        forget UI text source source in view
    set source's text to text
    set source's element to editor's node
    set view's selection to a new UI text selection
    set view's selection's anchor source and view's selection's caret source to source
    set view's selection's anchor to the UI text boundary at or before (buffer's anchor) in text
    set view's selection's caret to the UI text boundary at or before (buffer's caret) in text
    set view's keyboard focus to true
    set view's focus order to layout's order
    refresh UI focus in view
    set view's text focus to editor's node
    set view's reveal caret to false
    set layout's text scroll to buffer's horizontal
    set layout's scroll position to buffer's vertical
    set layout's scroll target to buffer's vertical
    set view's damaged to true

to [bind UI source document] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    require condition (document's available) reporting "An unavailable source cannot be opened"
    set buffer to the UI source buffer for document in editor
    if buffer != editor's current:
        remember the UI source location of editor in view
        if editor's document's writable:
            edit UI source document (editor's document) to ((the UI value for (editor's node) in (view's instance))'s text) at (view's seconds) seconds
        exchange UI text state for (editor's node) in view with (the address of (editor's current's state))
        if buffer's state's text != document's source:
            clear UI text state (the address of (buffer's state))
            set buffer's state's text to document's source
        exchange UI text state for (editor's node) in view with (the address of (buffer's state))
        set editor's current to buffer
        set editor's document to document
        set editor's colors revision to 0
        set editor's shown to false
        set UI control (editor's node) read only (editor's read only or (document's writable = false)) in (view's instance)
        set layout to the UI layout for element (editor's node) in (view's layout)
        require condition (layout != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "A source view is missing its layout"
        forget UI text source (the address of (layout's text source)) in view
        set layout's text source's text to document's source
        set layout's text scroll to buffer's horizontal
        set layout's scroll position and layout's scroll target to buffer's vertical

to [show UI source document] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    bind UI source document document in editor in view
    restore UI source location (editor's current) in editor in view

to [visit UI source document] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [selecting] {integer:anchor} [through] {integer:caret} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    remember the UI source location of editor in view
    set buffer to editor's current
    set location to @intrinsic("construct", UI source location, buffer, buffer's anchor, buffer's caret, buffer's horizontal, buffer's vertical, editor's locations)
    set editor's locations to storage for one slot initialized with location
    show UI source document document in editor in view
    set editor's current's anchor to anchor
    set editor's current's caret to caret
    restore UI source location (editor's current) in editor in view
    set view's reveal caret to true

to get [go back in UI source editor] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    loop while editor's locations != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source location):
        set location to editor's locations
        set editor's locations to location's next
        set buffer to location's buffer
        if buffer's document's available:
            show UI source document (buffer's document) in editor in view
            set buffer's anchor to location's anchor
            set buffer's caret to location's caret
            set buffer's horizontal to location's horizontal
            set buffer's vertical to location's vertical
            restore UI source location buffer in editor in view
            deallocate location
            return true
        deallocate location
    return false

to get [the UI text state for] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [in] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    if document = editor's document:
        return the address of ((the UI value for (editor's node) in instance)'s text state)
    set buffer to the UI source buffer for document in editor
    if buffer's state's text != document's source:
        clear UI text state (the address of (buffer's state))
        set buffer's state's text to document's source
    return the address of (buffer's state)

to get [the UI main source of] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI source workspace:workspace} [at] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds]:
    synchronize UI source workspace workspace at seconds seconds
    return editor's document's project's entry's source

# Replacement is a new editing session, even when the incoming bytes are equal.
# Snapshot borrowed input before releasing an active or parked state.
to [replace UI main source of] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [with] {string:text} [at] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds]:
    set content to text
    set main to editor's document's project's entry
    set buffer to the UI source buffer for main in editor
    set buffer's anchor and buffer's caret to 0
    set buffer's horizontal and buffer's vertical to 0.0
    if main = editor's document:
        set layout to the UI layout for element (editor's node) in (view's layout)
        require condition (layout != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "A source view is missing its layout"
        set focused to view's selection's caret source = (the address of (layout's text source))
        set replacement to a new UI text state
        set replacement's text to content
        exchange UI text state for (editor's node) in view with (the address of replacement)
        clear UI text state (the address of replacement)
        forget UI text source (the address of (layout's text source)) in view
        set layout's text source's text to content
        set layout's text scroll to 0.0
        set layout's scroll position and layout's scroll target to 0.0
        set editor's colors revision to 0
        set editor's shown to false
        if focused:
            restore UI source location buffer in editor in view
    else:
        clear UI text state (the address of (buffer's state))
        set buffer's state's text to content
    edit UI source document main to content at seconds seconds

to [load UI main source of] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [from] {string:text} [at] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds]:
    set layout to the UI layout for element (editor's node) in (view's layout)
    require condition (layout != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "A source view is missing its layout"
    set focused to view's selection's caret source = (the address of (layout's text source))
    replace UI main source of editor in view with text at seconds seconds
    free UI source locations (editor's locations)
    set editor's locations to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source location)
    bind UI source document (editor's document's project's entry) in editor in view
    if focused:
        restore UI source location (editor's current) in editor in view
